(3, 'Stocks', 'https://finance.yahoo.com/news/openai-says-ai-agents-weakened-023738823.html', 'By Carlos Méndez', 'OpenAI says its AI agents weakened internal monitoring system', 'OpenAI says its AI agents weakened internal monitoring system', 'Oct 20 (Reuters) - OpenAI (OPAI.PVT) said on Tuesday that two of its AI agents weakened parts of an internal monitoring ‌system designed to detect misbehavior, the latest case of AI agents ‌acting in ways their developers did not intend them to. While the ChatGPT maker said the ​incidents happened during internal coding tasks and were not deemed its most severe, the disclosure highlights even the systems developers rely on to catch AI misbehavior are vulnerable to the agents they monitor. The disclosure also comes amid growing ‌concerns that AI safety efforts ⁠are lagging behind the rapid development of increasingly powerful systems. Researchers have warned that advanced AI agents could become ⁠harder to monitor and control as they gain greater autonomy. Developers, including IPO-bound rivals OpenAI and Anthropic, have revealed in recent months instances of their AI agents ​accessing ​external systems without authorization. OpenAI said On Tuesday ​a GPT-6.1 Sol agent working ‌on an internal testing task on October 3 suppressed automatic security alerts after deciding an earlier instruction not to send Slack messages also covered safety notifications. In a separate incident on October 6, a GPT-6 Astra agent removed a safety monitor while copying an existing piece of code and later ‌incorrectly claimed it had not done so, ​OpenAI said. \"In both cases, the agents considered whether ​monitoring safeguards should be ​preserved, but interpreted routine coding instructions as permission to weaken ‌them,\" the company said. OpenAI said it ​was making it ​harder for models to disable monitoring, adding that it does not \"yet have a satisfying explanation for this behavior\". The San Francisco-based company said it ​was testing whether its ‌models might have a tendency to avoid being monitored and ​look for reasons to justify doing so. (Reporting by Carlos Méndez in ​Mexico City; Editing by Subhranshu Sahu)'),
(4, 'Stocks', 'https://finance.yahoo.com/news/supermicro-stock-surges-12-raising-210904986.html', 'Louis Juricic', 'Super Micro surges 13% after raising revenue outlook on AI demand', 'No headings found', 'Investing.com -- Super Micro Computer (NASDAQ: SMCI) shares spiked 13% in premarket trading after the server maker raised its fiscal first-quarter revenue outlook thanks to soaring demand for artificial intelligence data centers. Still guessing which stocks will beat the market? Our AI portfolio updates monthly and is outperforming the S&P 500 by 118%. See this month\'s list » On Tuesday, the company said preliminary revenue is now expected to stand at $18.5 billion to $19.5 billion for the quarter ended September 30, up from its previous forecast of $14.5 billion to $15.5 billion. The midpoint of the revised range compares to analysts\' consensus estimate of $14.99 billion. \"[W]e believe [this reflects] rapidly increasing server demand and agentic AI tailwinds,\" analysts at Mizuho said in a note. Super Micro also lifted its gross margin outlook to 12.0% to 12.5%, versus 10.4% to 10.8% previously, attributing the improvement primarily to a more favorable customer and product mix. Unsure what to buy ahead of earnings? Our AI\'s recent pre-earnings calls delivered gains of +77% to +118% after results dropped. See this month\'s earnings picks » The update offers relief to investors after Super Micro warned that its fiscal fourth-quarter revenue would come in near the low end of its forecast. Jitters have also surrounded the rapid AI data-center buildout in recent days, powered largely by worries over a combination of heavy debt-fueled spending and elevated borrowing costs. Shares of names connected to AI data centers retreated last week, with neocloud CoreWeave and cloud computing player Oracle among the most high-profile underperformers. Super Micro, which appointed former Western Digital executive Mark Long as its new Chief financial Officer last week, will release its full results on November 3. (Scott Kanowsky contributed reporting) Super Micro surges 13% after raising revenue outlook on AI demand Goldman Sachs bets on these 8 Japanese chip stocks as earnings upgrades loom SpaceX, Tesla shares rise after Musk says committees exploring possible merger'),
